{"name":"Lemures","hex":"#bfb9d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemures","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spirits or ghosts of the dead, considered as malignant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemures"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemures","blocks":[{"text":"The lemures were shades or spirits of the restless or malignant dead in Roman religion, sometimes used interchangeably with the term larvae .\nThe term lemures was first used by the Augustan poet Horace, and was the more common literary term during the Augustan era, with larvae being used only once by Horace. However, lemures is also uncommon: Ovid being the other main figure to employ it, in his Fasti, the six-book calendar poem on Roman holidays and religious customs.\nLater the two terms were used nearly or completely interchangeably, e.g. by St. Augustine in De Civitate Dei."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemures","wikidata":"Q20100888"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/500px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/1280px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/500px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg"}],"sounds":{"lemures":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/